cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "How good is a 4B open-weights local LLM for agentic DFT workflows? A reproducibility case study"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sharma
    given-names: Shambhu B.
license: MIT
# Data under data/ is CC-BY-4.0; see LICENSE-DATA.
repository-code: "https://github.com/shambhubhandari/Agentic-Workflow"
abstract: >-
  ACV reads published computational papers on pentagonal two-dimensional materials,
  extracts the claimed result together with the method used to produce it, and re-runs
  what can be re-run in SIESTA. An agentic layer translates each paper's stated method
  into SIESTA settings, drives the convergence loop, diagnoses failures, and reviews a
  finished calculation before a verdict is written. Verdicts describe the recomputation
  rather than the paper: there is deliberately no outcome meaning "verified" or "refuted".
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - density functional theory
  - SIESTA
  - two-dimensional materials
  - pentagonal monolayers
  - LLM agents
